.TH CYAML_DICTIONARY_REMOVE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_dictionary_remove \- remove and free a key from a dictionary node
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

ccol_retval_t cyaml_dictionary_remove(cyaml map, const char *key);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Remove the entry that carries this key from the dictionary node map.
The function then frees the value subtree of that entry recursively.
The other members keep their order.  A cyaml_dictionary_iter cursor
stays valid across the removal of any member other than the one that
its next step reads, the successor of the member that it stands on;
the removal of the current member is therefore allowed during a walk.
The removal of that successor invalidates the cursor.  See
cyaml_dictionary_first(3).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        - the function removed and freed the entry.
ccol_invalid_args   - map is NULL, or map is not CYAML_DICTIONARY.
ccol_key_not_found  - the dictionary holds no such key.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_dictionary_set (3),
.BR cyaml_dictionary_get (3),
.BR cyaml_dictionary_first (3),
.BR cyaml_list_remove (3)
